_models":["claude-fable-5-1"],"explanation":"**What the grid is made of.** Every input is a blank 15×15 canvas with a handful of single coloured pixels (3 or 4), each in its own row. The output keeps the same size and the same colours, but each pixel has grown into a large structure, so this is a drawing puzzle: each seed emits lines, and the canvas is partitioned between the seeds.\n\n**Reading the evidence.** The fact sheet lists the added cells as straight segments, and they come in three kinds:\n\n1. For every seed, a full horizontal line of its colour across its own row (the two \"right\" segments on each side of the seed, together with the seed, cover x=0..14).\n2. The leftmost and rightmost columns are coloured in vertical bands, one band per seed, stacked top to bottom in seed order (e.g. train 1: colour 2 on rows 0–5, colour 7 on rows 6–9, colour 8 on rows 10–14).\n3. The top row is completely filled with the topmost seed's colour and the bottom row with the bottommost seed's colour.\n\nThe only thing to pin down is where one side band ends and the next begins. Comparing with the seed rows: train 1 has seeds at rows 3, 7, 12 and boundaries after rows 5 and 9; train 2 has seeds at 1, 3, 7, 9 and boundaries after rows 2, 5, 8; train 3 has seeds at 2, 7, 9 with boundaries after 4 and 8; train 4 has seeds at 2, 4, 11 with boundaries after 3 and 7. In every case the last row of the upper band is `floor((y_upper + y_lower)/2)`: the midpoint between consecutive seeds, with an exact tie going to the upper seed (3 and 7 → 5; 7 and 12 → 9; 2 and 7 → 4; 4 and 11 → 7). So the side columns are split by nearest seed row, ties upward, and the first/last bands extend to the grid edges.\n\n**Construction (same for every input, including the test).** Sort the seeds by row. For each seed, draw its horizontal line across its row. Then for each seed compute its band `[start, end]` from the midpoints with its neighbours (first band starts at 0, last ends at the bottom), and paint columns 0 and 14 of that band with its colour. Finally fill row 0 with the first seed's colour and the last row with the last seed's colour.\n\nFor the test input the seeds are 8 at row 2, 2 at row 4, 1 at row 9, 3 at row 12. Bands: 8 on rows 0–3 ((2+4)/2 = 3), 2 on rows 4–6 ((4+9)/2 = 6), 1 on rows 7–10 ((9+12)/2 = 10), 3 on rows 11–14. Full rows: 2 (8), 4 (2), 9 (1), 12 (3), plus row 0 in 8 and row 14 in 3.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n\n    # seeds: single pixels, one per row; sort by row\n    seeds = sorted([(y, x, int(g[y, x])) for y in range(H) for x in range(W) if g[y, x] != bg])\n    if not seeds:\n        emit(out, \"no seeds; nothing to draw\")\n        return out\n\n    # stage 1: each seed emits a full horizontal line of its colour through its row\n    for y, x, c in seeds:\n        out[y, :] = c\n    emit(out, \"each seed pixel is extended to a full horizontal line of its colour across its own row\")\n\n    # stage 2: left and right columns split into bands by nearest seed row (ties go up)\n    n = len(seeds)\n    for i, (y, x, c) in enumerate(seeds):\n        start = 0 if i == 0 else (seeds[i - 1][0] + y) // 2 + 1\n        end = H - 1 if i == n - 1 else (y + seeds[i + 1][0]) // 2\n        out[start:end + 1, 0] = c\n        out[start:end + 1, W - 1] = c\n    emit(out, \"left and right border columns are painted in bands, each band belonging to the nearest seed row (midpoints between consecutive seeds, ties to the upper seed)\")\n\n    # stage 3: top row takes the topmost seed colour, bottom row the bottommost\n    out[0, :] = seeds[0][2]\n    out[H - 1, :] = seeds[-1][2]\n    emit(out, \"top row filled with the topmost seed's colour and bottom row with the bottommost seed's colour, closing the frames\")\n\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"selection":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The output keeps the same size and the same colours, but each pixel has grown into a large structure, so this is a drawing puzzle: each seed emits lines, and the canvas is partitioned between the seeds."}],"rays":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"each seed pixel is extended to a full horizontal line of its colour across its own row"}],"order":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**Construction (same for every input, including the test).** Sort the seeds by row."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"5f02ad9b9dd03d9ed54b4852cd575b0ff50965fff39ad205e03c45f1470df83a","task_sha256":"440525e023121d4444055a284b6081b7b26bfa73e3dbcde9de46879af8713f4f","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
